# cases the spirv column cannot serve: a case name per line, then the reason.
# entries are written out by name rather than globbed by family, so a case added
# later inherits nothing and has to be reviewed against this file on its way in.
#
# two kinds of entry live here and they are not interchangeable.
#
#   TARGET LIMITATION. SPIR-V cannot express the construct. the corpus has no
#   question to ask, and the entry stays until the target or the language changes.
#
#   MACH DEFECT. SPIR-V can express the construct and mach does not emit it, either
#   refusing to build or writing a module spirv-val rejects. the corpus has a
#   question and mach cannot yet answer it. every one of these names an issue and is
#   deleted by the change that closes it, not by anyone tidying this file.
#
# 84 of the 115 cases build, validate and carry the column. the 31 under TARGET
# LIMITATION cannot be expressed by the target, and MACH DEFECT is empty. mem/rec_layout passes a subobject of
# a local record by reference, which spirv-val rejects at O0 (an OpAccessChain result
# as an OpFunctionCall pointer operand, checked against spv1.0 through vulkan1.3);
# at O2 the call is inlined and the case carries the column, and O2 is what the
# column builds.

# ---- TARGET LIMITATION ----

call/call_recursive  a SPIR-V execution model has no call stack, so a function may not be reachable from itself: "this call graph is a cycle and the SPIR-V target cannot express it: descend -> descend". recursion at four shapes is what the case is, so there is nothing to narrow.
call/call_arg_capture  same refusal as cmp/short_circuit. a later argument writing a module-scope record is one of the writers the case proves the capture against (#3460).
call/call_chain  same refusal, "chain -> chain". the case holds values live across a self-recursive chain by construction.
call/call_indirect  "unsupported parameter 1 of type `fun(i64, i64) i64` in the SPIR-V Logical Shader environment: logical addressing has no function pointers, so a function value cannot cross a call". the parameter is a function value, so the target cannot take the case's whole subject.
cmp/short_circuit  "a plain module-scope variable is not reachable from the SPIR-V target: a shader has no general global storage, so a module-scope `val` / `var` reaches a stage only by carrying an interface role". the case proves non-evaluation through side-effect counters, which have to be module-scope state.
ct/by_memory  "#[oblivious] function `corpus.cases.ct.by_memory.vx` cannot be compiled for the `spirv` target: its back half emits a module for a downstream compiler to translate rather than the instructions that execute". secrets crossing an oblivious call through memory are the case.
ct/mul_serial  "#[oblivious] function `corpus.cases.ct.mul_serial.serial8` cannot be compiled for the `spirv` target: its back half emits a module for a downstream compiler to translate rather than the instructions that execute". secret arithmetic in an oblivious function is the case.
ct/mul_secret  "secret value used as an operand of a variable-latency integer multiply". SPIR-V declares no data-independent multiply, and the secret multiply is the case.
ct/mul_secret128  same refusal, and its 128-bit product type is not realized on spirv either (#3511).
ct/shift_secret  "secret value used as a variable shift count on a target without a barrel shifter". SPIR-V declares no constant-time variable shift, and the secret count is the case; the oblivious functions would be refused for the same reason as ct/mul_serial after it.
int128/arith  "a 128-bit integer is not realized on spirv: the target declares no integer of that width". SPIR-V integer types are 8, 16, 32 and 64 bits wide and the target emits a module for a downstream compiler, so it declares no wider integer and no lane plan realizes one (#3511, ruling Q8).
int128/mul  "a 128-bit integer is not realized on spirv: the target declares no integer of that width". SPIR-V integer types are 8, 16, 32 and 64 bits wide and the target emits a module for a downstream compiler, so it declares no wider integer and no lane plan realizes one (#3511, ruling Q8).
int128/convert_int128  "a 128-bit integer is not realized on spirv: the target declares no integer of that width". SPIR-V integer types are 8, 16, 32 and 64 bits wide and the target emits a module for a downstream compiler, so it declares no wider integer and no lane plan realizes one (#3511, ruling Q8).
int128/cmp_int128  "a 128-bit integer is not realized on spirv: the target declares no integer of that width". SPIR-V integer types are 8, 16, 32 and 64 bits wide and the target emits a module for a downstream compiler, so it declares no wider integer and no lane plan realizes one (#3511, ruling Q8).
int128/call_int128  "a 128-bit integer is not realized on spirv: the target declares no integer of that width". SPIR-V integer types are 8, 16, 32 and 64 bits wide and the target emits a module for a downstream compiler, so it declares no wider integer and no lane plan realizes one (#3511, ruling Q8).
int128/divrem  "a 128-bit integer is not realized on spirv: the target declares no integer of that width". SPIR-V integer types are 8, 16, 32 and 64 bits wide and the target emits a module for a downstream compiler, so it declares no wider integer and no lane plan realizes one (#3511, ruling Q8).
int128/shift  "a 128-bit integer is not realized on spirv: the target declares no integer of that width". SPIR-V integer types are 8, 16, 32 and 64 bits wide and the target emits a module for a downstream compiler, so it declares no wider integer and no lane plan realizes one (#3511, ruling Q8).
int128/call_vector  "a 128-bit integer is not realized on spirv: the target declares no integer of that width". the case passes that type beside a vector.
int128/vector_reinterpret  "a 128-bit integer is not realized on spirv: the target declares no integer of that width". the case reinterprets that type to and from a vector.
mem/global_data  same refusal. module-scope initialized storage is the case.
mem/escaping_element  same refusal as mem/ptr_arith. the callee reads the siblings of the element it is handed, and pointer arithmetic is the case (#3482).
mem/global_zero  same refusal. module-scope zero-initialized storage is the case.
mem/agg_overlap  same refusal as mem/ptr_arith. overlapping records are carved out of one buffer by pointer arithmetic, and their overlap is the case (#4235).
mem/ptr_arith  "pointer arithmetic across whole objects is not supported by the SPIR-V target: a logical pointer names one object, so a getelementptr's leading index may only be 0". the pointer-to-scalar parameter itself is accepted (#2940); bump then indexes off it, and pointer arithmetic is the case.
vec/load_literal  same refusal as mem/ptr_arith. every probe indexes a pointer-to-scalar parameter at a variable offset, and the literal of consecutive loads it folds is the case (#3753).
vec/range  same refusal as mem/ptr_arith. the load and store probes range a pointer-to-scalar parameter at a variable offset, and one vector load or store through that address is the case.
vec/split  same refusal as mem/ptr_arith. every probe reads its operands from a byte buffer at an offset, reinterpreted as a vector pointer. spir-v splits nothing (its vectors are values, not registers), and vec/vec_f32x8 carries a wide vector on the column.
vec/global_loop  same refusal as mem/ptr_arith, and same refusal as mem/global_data: every probe reads its operand vectors through a pointer at a variable index against a module-scope global, and both are the case (#4151).
mem/uni_layout  "unsupported parameter 2 of type `uni{f32, i32, i32, [4]i8}` in the SPIR-V Logical Shader environment: SPIR-V has no untyped union, so a raw union has no type to declare". a raw union read back through a second member is the case.

# ---- MACH DEFECT ----

# #2923 (more than sixteen parameters) and #2940 (a pointer to a record as a
# parameter) closed with the value-oriented module ABI (#2963); call/call_mixed
# and mem/rec_layout carry the column. #3275 (a three-way
# early-return chain inlined twice or into a loop) closed with the structurizer's
# forward merge for a selection whose arms leave through one block;
# cmp/ret_chain_inline carries the column.

